,"chapterId":"el-b49-c2","topicId":"el-b49-t2579-0","type":"mcq","text":"Prime factorization of 16 is","options":["2 × 8","1 × 16","2 × 2 × 2 × 2","2 × 4 × 2"],"correctIndex":2,"page":33,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-57422572777a3b70","chapterId":"el-b49-c2","topicId":"el-b49-t2580-0","type":"mcq","text":"The LCM of 33, 66 and 81 is","options":["1770","1872","1782","1287"],"correctIndex":2,"page":36,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-5c8333081a3e01b6","chapterId":"el-b49-c2","topicId":"el-b49-t2580-0","type":"mcq","text":"The LCM of two or more prime numbers is always equal to their","options":["Prime Factor","Quotient","LCM","Product"],"correctIndex":3,"page":36,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-41017872a04135e9","chapterId":"el-b49-c3","topicId":"el-b49-t3239-1","type":"mcq","text":"1 / 3 + 2 / 5 is equal to","options":["3 / 5","11 / 15","3 / 8","2 / 15"],"correctIndex":1,"page":44,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn","reviewNote":"1/3 + 2/5 = 11/15; no official option was correct","explanation":"1/3 + 2/5 = 11/15."},{"id":"el-b49-elq-763bb417413ffc11","chapterId":"el-b49-c3","topicId":"el-b49-t3314-1","type":"mcq","text":"2 / 3 - 5 / 9 is equal to","options":["3 / 9","7 / 3","1 / 9","7 / 9"],"correctIndex":2,"page":46,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-9db242f7cada928b","chapterId":"el-b49-c3","topicId":"el-b49-t3240-1","type":"mcq","text":"The product of 3 / 4 and 4 / 3 is","options":["1000","10","1","111"],"correctIndex":2,"page":49,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-e9a10ef639fff6f2","chapterId":"el-b49-c3","topicId":"el-b49-t3240-1","type":"mcq","text":"In ________ the order of the fractions does not affect the result.","options":["addition and subtraction","subtraction and divisions","multiplication and division","addition and multiplication"],"correctIndex":3,"page":49,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn","reviewNote":"order does not matter in addition and multiplication; official answer was multiplication and division","explanation":"Order does not matter in addition and multiplication."},{"id":"el-b49-elq-97d6c1b19fa6c2a0","chapterId":"el-b49-c4","topicId":"el-b49-t2583-0","type":"mcq","text":"While putting ________ at the right of a decimal does not effect its value","options":["100","0","1","10"],"correctIndex":1,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-52775fd349d3c74c","chapterId":"el-b49-c4","topicId":"el-b49-t2583-0","type":"mcq","text":"When multiply a decimal by 100, we move decimal point 2 places to the _______","options":["left","down","up","right"],"correctIndex":3,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-0f340824ac2e27ab","chapterId":"el-b49-c4","topicId":"el-b49-t2879-0","type":"mcq","text":"We represent percentage by the symbol","options":["≤","ϕ","÷","%"],"correctIndex":3,"page":78,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-810df1b9ec5f8f3f","chapterId":"el-b49-c4","topicId":"el-b49-t2879-0","type":"mcq","text":"Percentage is a special kind of fraction whose denominator is always ________","options":["1","10","100","1000"],"correctIndex":2,"page":78,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-ac4d6eaf74a96222","chapterId":"el-b49-c4","topicId":"el-b49-t3251-1","type":"mcq","text":"20% of 540 is ________","options":["37","108","27","270"],"correctIndex":1,"page":80,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-4cd206b59324d1be","chapterId":"el-b49-c5","topicId":"el-b49-t3253-1","type":"mcq","text":"There are _______ metres in 2 kilometres.","options":["500","1000","200","2000"],"correctIndex":3,"page":88,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-df13aacd9f0d95f3","chapterId":"el-b49-c5","topicId":"el-b49-t2590-0","type":"mcq","text":"To measure _______ hours, minutes and seconds are used.","options":["Time","Distance","Area","Length"],"correctIndex":0,"page":95,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b49-elq-f4c61088c19ee8d1","chapterId":"el-b